 RESULT: PASS — the handshake works end to end. This run did NOT involve Wine.
         the second process was: /opt/data/neuralscreen-linux/.venv/bin/python /opt/data/neuralscreen-linux/experiments/mmap_bridge/fake_windows.py /tmp/nsb_bridge/frame.bin
         so the layout and the protocol are proven; that Wine shares the pages is NOT proven by this run.

  1.0 MB written and returned in 3.61ms mean over 3 rounds (553 MB/s both ways)
  of which 0.74ms is our own write (1355 MB/s one way)
  (no msync per round: two MAP_SHARED mappings of one file are the same physical pages, so a per-frame flush would be paid for nothing)

  for scale: a pipe read measured ~1100 MB/s on the analysis box,
  and the MVP's 2560x1440 floor with NGX skipped is ~85ms a frame.
